/target
.scratch/
.claude/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store

# drft runs here as a local authoring aid, not as repo tooling. Neither the
# config nor the lockfile is tracked: a clone gets no graph, CI checks nothing,
# and staleness is a fact about a maintainer's working tree rather than a claim
# this repository makes. Ignored here rather than in a personal exclude file
# because the choice is deliberate and worth stating where anyone can read it.
#
# Anchored to the root on purpose. The project may add other tracked state under
# `.drft` later, so ignore the two files this repository keeps local rather than
# the entire directory.
/.drft/config.toml
/.drft/lock.toml

# Each project under examples/ is its own graph and ships its own config, which
# has to be tracked. Re-included explicitly because a machine-wide ignore of the
# state directory would otherwise swallow them: the ones already tracked survive, and
# a newly added example would not.
!examples/*/.drft/
!examples/*/.drft/config.toml

# An example's lockfile is not. Each example's README walks a reader through
# `drft lock --all` against it, so running the docs writes one — a generated
# artifact of trying the tool, which should no more be committed than the root
# lockfile is. The root entries are anchored, so they do not reach these.
examples/*/.drft/lock.toml
